%SIXMD 1
# @?PRIME - TEST AN 18-BIT INTEGER FOR PRIMALITY

## DESCRIPTION

PRINTS PRIME OR COMPOSITE. RETURNS SUCCESS FOR PRIME, FAILURE FOR COMPOSITE, AND STATUS 2 FOR INVALID INPUT.

USAGE IS 'PRIME NUMBER'.

THIS COMMAND IS IMPLEMENTED ENTIRELY IN PDP-6 ASSEMBLER AND IS PART OF THE
OPTIONAL ASMUTILS PACKAGE. IT IS INSTALLED IN /OPTION/BASE/EXEC.

## @?FILES

### @?/OPTION/BASE/EXEC/PRIME
OPTIONAL EXECUTABLE.

### @?/OPTION/BASE/SOURCE/ASMUTILS/PRIME.S
ASSEMBLER SOURCE.

